+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"The bug: buttons with duplicate light indices (e.g. `[0,0]`) or pressing the same light twice. In a *toggle* puzzle, toggling a light twice = no effect (mod 2), so `[0,0]` is a no-op button. But my column construction ORs bits, so duplicates cancel out correctly in the matrix... but the issue: `[[0,0]]` toggles light 0 twice → net no toggle. My matrix sets column bit 0 (since `|=` then `|=` same bit → still set once = toggles once). That's the bug: duplicates should XOR/cancel, not OR.\n\nIn the toggle model, a button toggles each listed light; if a light appears twice, it's toggled twice = off. So the coefficient is the *parity* of occurrences, not OR. Let me fix: use XOR instead of OR when building columns."}}
